                <pb facs="0376" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/10002: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wallace</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-16T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1122. Your 1274, June 10, 10 P.M. Mission.</p>
                <p>Department concurs in general with spirit of note and with specific demands, but
                    suggests modification at two points. 1. Statement <pb facs="0377" n="287"
                        xml:id="pg287"/> that “Powers renounce any claim to raise objections of
                    principle” unnecessarily sweeping especially as United States is not party to
                    treaty. Suggest change after Powers “do not desire at present to raise
                    objections”. 2. Last paragraph, section 4, suggest insertion after interference
                    “other than that authorized by general laws in accordance with letter and spirit
                    of this note”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
